---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy | PTPN">
  <section style="padding-block:96px 72px"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top:18px;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px)">Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="legal"><h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>PTPN ("we") is a personal training business run by Pedro, based in Bush Hill Park, Enfield, London. Contact: <a href="mailto:info@ptpn.co.uk" style="color:var(--gold)">info@ptpn.co.uk</a>.</p>
<h2>What we collect and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Enquiry form data</strong>: your name, email, optional phone, and what you tell us about your goal. Used only to reply to you and, if you become a client, to coach you.</li>
  <li><strong>App and coaching data</strong>: workouts, nutrition logs, measurements, check-ins, chat and progress photos. Some of this is health data (special category under UK GDPR); we process it only with your explicit, dated consent, given in the app.</li>
  <li><strong>No advertising trackers, no analytics cookies.</strong> The website is static and only loads the fonts it needs.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Where it is stored</h2>
<p>Data is stored with Supabase (EU infrastructure, Dublin region). Transactional email is processed by Resend. We do not sell or share your data with third parties for marketing. Staff: it is just the coach.</p>
<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>Enquiries we never correspond with are deleted after 12 months. Client records are kept while you coach with us and, if you consent, for up to 6 years afterwards because trainers are expected to keep records of training delivered. Progress photos are yours, delete them any time from the app, or ask and we delete them.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection. Email the address above and you will get a reply within one month. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO).</p>
<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Accounts are password protected with row-level access: you can only ever read your own data. Photos are stored in a private bucket, never public URLs.</p>
<p style="margin-top:26px">Last updated: 28 October 2026.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal{margin-top:30px;color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;line-height:1.75}
  .legal h2{font-size:19px;color:var(--ink);margin:34px 0 10px;letter-spacing:0}
  .legal p,.legal li{margin-bottom:12px}
  .legal ul{padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:6px}
</style>
